  "storyPrologue1": "A sleepy seaside town. A little bakery with a faded sign: Sugarleaf.",
  "storyPrologue2": "Grandma, I'm home... I'll take care of your bakery now.",
  "storyPrologue3": "Her recipe book! But so many pages are missing...",
  "storyPrologue4": "Let's start with something simple. Cupcakes!",
  "storyHoa1Line1": "The lights are on at Sugarleaf again. You must be little Mai.",
  "storyHoa1Line2": "Yes! Did you know my grandma?",
  "storyHoa1Line3": "Every Sunday for forty years. Her egg tarts... I still miss them.",
  "storyHoa1Line4": "Then I'll learn to make them for you. I promise!",
  "storyLinh1Line1": "Hi! I'm Linh. I study at the art school up the hill.",
  "storyLinh1Line2": "I draw every pastry I eat. Your shop is SO cute!",
  "storyLinh1Line3": "Then I'd better make them pretty for you!",
  "storyHoa2Line1": "Mr. Hoa! I found the egg tart page today.",
  "storyHoa2Line2": "Then today is a good day. Let's see if your hands remember her.",
  "storyHoa2Line3": "I'll do my best!",
  "storyKenji1Line1": "Hello. I'm Kenji. I travel and photograph small towns.",
  "storyKenji1Line2": "I'm not sure what I want. Something that feels like a sunny morning?",
  "storyKenji1Line3": "A sunny morning... Strawberry cake, I think!",
  "storyLinh2Line1": "Mai, can you make macarons? They're my favorite thing to draw!",
  "storyLinh2Line2": "They're tricky... but let's try together.",
  "storyLinh2Line3": "Yay! I'll sketch while you bake!",
  "storyKenji2Line1": "Tomorrow I'll climb the lighthouse at dawn. I need some courage.",
  "storyKenji2Line2": "Courage tastes bold and a little sweet. Red velvet!",
  "storyKenji2Line3": "You read moods like recipes.",
  "storyHoa3Line1": "I brought something. She gave me this page years ago, for safekeeping.",
  "storyHoa3Line2": "Grandma's handwriting... Thank you, Mr. Hoa.",
  "storyHoa3Line3": "It belongs in this kitchen. Just like you.",
  "storyLinh3Line1": "Look! My drawing of your shop won a prize at school!",
  "storyLinh3Line2": "It's beautiful, Linh! Can I hang it by the window?",
  "storyLinh3Line3": "Only if we celebrate with a matcha cake!",
  "storyKenji3Line1": "My photos of this town will be shown in a gallery in Tokyo.",
  "storyKenji3Line2": "I want to remember it with something calm and rich.",
  "storyKenji3Line3": "Then cheesecake, with blueberries like the sea.",
  "storyFinaleLine1": "Mr. Hoa, Linh, Kenji... this bakery feels alive again.",
  "storyFinaleLine2": "Grandma's book still has empty pages. I'll fill them, one by one.",
  "storyCh1End1": "The first pages of Grandma's book are filled again.",
  "storyCh1End2": "The town is starting to know my cupcakes… Time to get busier!",
  "storyCh2End3": "And just past the back door, a new chapter is waiting…",
  "storyCh3Open1": "Behind the bakery, Grandma's garden has grown wild with mint and climbing roses.",
  "storyCh3Open2": "What's hiding under all these leaves? A little garden shed!",
  "storyCh3Open3": "A page from Grandma's book, tucked in a flowerpot: \"Croissants. Fold the butter in, and be patient.\"",
  "storyCh3Open4": "Mai brushes off the soil and smiles. The garden kept Grandma's secret safe.",
  "storyMochi1Line1": "Rain drums on the awning. Beneath it, a small grey cat sits very, very still.",
  "storyMochi1Line2": "Oh! You're soaked, little one. Come in, the oven is warm.",
  "storyMochi1Line3": "The cat curls up by the counter and purrs like a tiny engine.",
  "storyMochi1Line4": "I'll call you Mochi. Come by whenever it rains, okay?",
  "storyKenji4Line1": "Today I'd like something… for a day when you miss home.",
  "storyKenji4Line2": "Something small and warm, then. Like a hug from far away.",
  "storyKenji4Line3": "A madeleine. Grandma said one bite can bring back a whole afternoon.",
  "storyKenji4Line4": "Then I'll eat it slowly.",
  "storyCh4Open1": "Upstairs, dust dances in the light of the little round window.",
  "storyCh4Open2": "Grandma's old letter box… she kept every note her customers ever wrote.",
  "storyCh4Open3": "And two more pages: éclairs, and a fruit tart \"for sunny days\".",
  "storyCh4Open4": "Mai tucks the pages into the book. It feels a little heavier now, in the best way.",
  "storyRosa1Line1": "Good afternoon, dear. Your grandmother baked my wedding cake, you know.",
  "storyRosa1Line2": "Now my granddaughter is getting married, right by the sea.",
  "storyRosa1Line3": "Mrs. Rosa, that's wonderful news!",
  "storyRosa1Line4": "When the day comes, I'll order her cake from you. Your grandmother would like that.",
  "storyLinh4Line1": "Mai! The school fair is next week, and I signed us up for a stall!",
  "storyLinh4Line2": "Us? What are we selling?",
  "storyLinh4Line3": "Apple pie! The whole school smells of cinnamon when someone brings one.",
  "storyLinh4Line4": "Then we'll bake the prettiest lattice in town. Grandma's way.",
  "storyCh5Open1": "Lanterns are going up all along the harbor. The seaside festival is almost here.",
  "storyCh5Open2": "The whole town is decorating… and everyone keeps asking about mooncakes.",
  "storyCh5Open3": "Grandma's book has a page for those too: lotus paste and a little flower press.",
  "storyCh5Open4": "Tonight the bakery will glow like one more lantern by the sea.",
  "storyHoa4Line1": "Every winter, your grandmother baked a chocolate log for the whole street.",
  "storyHoa4Line2": "Little meringue mushrooms, a dusting of sugar snow… the children adored it.",
  "storyHoa4Line3": "A bûche de Noël? I've never made one.",
  "storyHoa4Line4": "You will. Her hands are in yours now, I can tell.",
  "storyRosa2Line1": "The wedding is today, dear. Is the cake ready?",
  "storyRosa2Line2": "Almost. Three tiers, wrapped as a gift, just like the one Grandma made for you.",
  "storyRosa2Line3": "Oh… my granddaughter will cry. I might cry too.",
  "storyRosa2Line4": "Then let's make it worth every happy tear.",
  "storyFinale2Line1": "The last empty page of Grandma's book is finally filled.",
  "storyFinale2Line2": "The bakery is warm and busy again, full of friends and their stories.",
  "storyFinale2Line3": "But a good bakery never runs out of stories… there are many more to come.",

